s stage she  can't give us specific policies  well she did give specific policies on  uh growth there's a a focus on uh  reducing the fuel uh price of fuel  straight away on increasing tax  thresholds these would be done  immediately but she also gave him to say  that and i think this will apply to any  leader that whoever then comes in is  going to have to probably have an  emergency budget uh in the autumn to  look at where we go  as a nation the cost of living crisis is  serious we need to look at our fiscal  policies what we can do to greater  support the british  people and it's not going to be simply  done by borrowing huge sums of money  which is going to cause more problems in  the longer term  but can you understand the people  watching last night looked looked penny  more than heard what she said and  thought this is being very vague it's  just vague comments how can we actually  now vote for vague comments  well you won't be voting for vague  comments at all you've been voting for  manifestos don't forget this is about  there were three audiences here that  were watching this not just mps party  members the nation as well uh there will  be plenty of opportunity to spell out  not just an economic policy but that on  the nhs  as well that was the other the third big  question that came up is how we're going  to pay for this  it was a great reality check i think for  our party to face the british people and  hear directly what needs to happen  on defense spending in particular i know  this is something that you're keen on  very vague as well she said she'd keep  2.5 but there may be an uptick i mean do  you think  that she should be as specific as others  of being and say yes 3 that's what we're  going for  well  you're absolutely right it didn't come  up last night britain's place in the  world then one of the things that  attracts me about penny morden is the  fact that it should be determined to  make sure that we do have a greater  voice and more coordinated voice on the  international stage there's an absence  of leadership in europe at the moment in  focusing on what do we do with ukraine  we're doing enough to make sure they  don't lose we're not enough to make sure  they win we don't have a policy on  russia what i understand and have got  confirmed from the penny board camp  is that we will be looking at  the state of our armed forces and making  sure that they have the competence to  meet the challenging threats i make it  very clear to all candidates i know  penny understands this the next 10 years  is going to be very very difficult  indeed security wise we are going to  have to spend more on defense you can  throw these numbers out like 2.5 percent  but ultimately you need to look at what  our capabilities are right now the  shortfalls particularly uh in uh  stockpiles of weapon systems and  ammunition we're going to have to review  that and that will have to happen  probably in the autumn as well just um  to end with briefly i want to talk to  you about this blue on blue fighting and  in particular one area and there has  been a lot of criticism about penny  mordant being a naval reservist i've  i've actually heard it being called  camouflage camouflage cosplay tom huden  heart an army reservist he has not  suffered the same  what do you think about that  i'm just really sorry that uh again  we're stooping to some of those levels  that you  see i mean i've been very careful even  in this interview absolutely i'm  supporting penny morden but i have huge  respect for my other uh colleagues as  well at the other flip side of this we  need to rally round the next prime  minister and make sure that we can show  the british people that we've learned  the lessons on discipline on focus on  vision of where we want to take the  nation and when we do these sort of  things and this blue on blue it actually  takes us the other way it actually  reduces our standing  within the british people as well penny  more than served continues to serve her  country uh from a uh military capacity  and she wants to do that now on the  national stage as well let's keep this  campaign positive let's focus on what  british people actually need rather than  actually taking chunks out of each other  okay mr wood thanks a lot for talking to  us  thank you

